  "slug": "logic-coach-for-teams",
  "title": "Question Believability",
  "description": "When evaluating arguments: - Focus on logic: Ask, \"Does this follow from the premises?\" instead of, \"Do I agree with the conclusion?\" - Separate belief from evidence: Analyze whether the conclusion feels true because it’s logical or just because it aligns with your beliefs. - Test counterexamples: Find a scenario where the logic works but the conclusion isn’t believable. Example: Someone says, \"All successful people wake up at 5 a.m.\" Instead of agreeing because it feels motivating, test the logic and exceptions.",
